  "note": "Lunenburg Primary School: page 124 carries Christina Guertin's Primary principal's report and this page carries the roster, whose sections (Pre-School, Kindergarten, First Grade Teachers) fix the school. Two columns, left x=0.190-0.202 and right x=0.387-0.392 in the OCR word boxes. Left column encodes name-then-role ('Krissy Carbone - Admin Secty'); the right column encodes a section heading followed by bare names, so most right-column entries carry role_raw ''. CONVENTION: a line holding a heading in one column and an entry in the other is listed under 'entries' only, so that every line number appears exactly once; the heading text still governs the entries beneath it via grade_or_dept. Lines 5, 13 and 21 hold headings in both columns (or in one with the other blank) and are the only heading-only lines. THE TOP OF THE ROSTER IS NOT ON THIS PAGE: the highest word box is at y=0.981, so the school name, the principal and the right column's own opening heading are above the crop. That is why lines 1-4 carry grade_or_dept '' -- and why the right column opens at '2C-Sara Kenney'. The likely reading is a Second Grade Teachers section (2A and 2B and 2E would have been above), but no such heading is on this page and none is asserted here. The Kindergarten lines print a class code before the name -- KI, K2, K3, K4, K5, K6 on lines 22, 24, 26, 28, 30 and 32 respectively (the first is OCR'd 'KI', most likely K1). role_raw records only the printed role word 'Teacher', because no single printed substring carries both. OCR damage kept verbatim: line 14 'rittanv Penoll- _eache' (likely 'Brittany Penoll - Teacher') and line 15 'aurene Broden - Par' (likely 'Laurene Broden - Para'). Line 17's right column prints the heading 'Reading Specialist' with a vertical gap below it where a name line would sit (y=0.648, next right-column box y=0.611) -- the name appears to have been lost, so it is recorded as an entry with name ''. Line 42 is the printed page number 123."
